UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfunfestivalatgaverfarm20763-20260904@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261019T165505Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Fall Fun Festival at Gaver Farm
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the vibrant colors and crisp air of autumn at the Fall Fun Festival at Gaver Farm! Running throughout September and October\, this family-friendly event offers over 65 exciting attractions\, making it the perfect destination for a day of fun\, laughter\, and unforgettable memories. Explore the Corn Maze. It’s a 7-acre corn maze\, perfect for all ages. This maze combines the thrill of exploration with the joy of discovery. Whether you’re working together as a family or racing against friends\, our corn maze promises a day of fun and excitement. Meet Our Friendly Barnyard Animals: Get up close and personal with our friendly barnyard animals\, including goats\, sheep\, cow\, alpacas\, pigs\, donkey\, pony\, bunnies\, peacocks\, turkeys\, ducks and chickens. Kids (and adults!) love the opportunity to feed and interact with our goats\, creating cherished memories and learning about farm life along the way. Fall Fun Fest Admission is $20.50 per person on September weekends\, $24.00 per person on October weekends\, and $14.50 per person on weekdays. Kids under 24 months are free. Tickets are available online and in person at the farm.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/fall-fun-festival-at-gaver-farm/20763/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventsummersfarmfallfestival12916-20260926@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261019T165505Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Summers Farm Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our annual Fall Festival at Summers Farm! For over 30 years\, Summers Farm has been the go-to destination for fall fun in Frederick County\, Maryland. With 45+ exciting activities\, there’s something for everyone to enjoy! Whether you're planning a day of family fun\, a corporate outing\, a school field trip\, an adventurous day date\, or just some good old-fashioned fun—Summers Farm is the place to be this fall! Here's what we have planned: Pumpkin Train Photo Ops Specialty Food & Drinks Famous Corn Maze Petting Zoo Wagon Rides Pedal Car Track Giant Slides Local Food Vendors 45+ Attractions & so much more! September 26 – November 1 September Sat – Sun: 10am – 7pm October 1 – 4 Thurs – Sun: 1pm – 7pm (Thurs)\, 1pm – 9pm (Fri)\, 10am – 9pm (Sat)\, 10am – 7pm (Sun) October 7 – 31 Wed – Thurs: 1pm – 7pm Fri: 1pm – 9pm Sat: 10am – 9pm Sun: 10am – 7pm November 1 (Sunday only) 10am – 7pm *October 12\, 16 & 26th – School Daze Craze: 11:30am – 9pm
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/summers-farm-fall-festival/12916/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventpumpkinpatchatmaynes24117-20261001@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261019T165505Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Pumpkin Patch At Mayne's
DESCRIPTION:Pumpkin Patch At Mayne's Celebrate Fall at Mayne's Tree Farm Pumpkin Patch in Frederick\, MD. Our pumpkin patch is open for the month of October on weekdays from 10a.m. - 6p.m. and on the weekends from 10a.m. - 5p.m. Pumpkins are available in small\, medium and large. Large groups by appointment during the week. Click Here for our full events schedule on facebook! Fall Activities Include: Hayrides To The Patch Corn Maze Apple Cider Scarecrow Making Straw Jumpin Antique Tractor Display For Your Fall Decoration Needs We Offer: Gourds ~ Mini Pumpkins ~ Indian Corn ~ Corn Stalks ~ Straw Bales
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/pumpkin-patch-at-maynes/24117/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventbackfromthedeadcemeterywalk8942-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261019T165505Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Back from the Dead Cemetery Walk
DESCRIPTION:On this unique and popular Cemetery Walk\, as a guide leads you through the dark by candlelight\, saints and other characters come to life and reflect upon the “Last Things”: death\, judgement\, heaven\, and hell. Through these encounters you’ll discover what it means to truly be alive\, both now and in the life to come. This faith-filled walk is ideal for youth groups and families with older children (14+). What to expect on the outdoor Cemetery Walk: This walking experience lasts for 1 hour and takes place primarily in the dark. All paths are wheelchair / stroller accessible. No seating is available throughout the experience. In the event of inclement weather\, all tickets will be refunded or rescheduled to another night\, pending availability.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/back-from-the-dead-cemetery-walk/8942/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventlegends26lore26224-20261009@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261019T165505Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Legends & Lore
DESCRIPTION:Come see the darker side of Frederick. When night falls\, Frederick’s familiar streets have rather different stories to tell. Climb aboard our vintage double-decker for an hour of dark tales from Frederick’s past\, researched from local histories\, old accounts and the legends that have lingered long after the people involved have gone. As we make our way through the city\, we’ll slow down at the very places connected to these stories\, from historic streets and old buildings to some of Frederick’s more famously haunted places. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of strange happenings\, restless spirits and the darker chapters of local history\, all told against the backdrop of Frederick after dark. And because it’s October\, you’ll also get a rather good view from the top deck as the city’s historic homes and neighborhoods put on their best autumn and Halloween displays. Whether you’re a believer\, a skeptic\, or simply enjoy a good story with a slightly unsettling ending\, Legends and Lore offers a different way to discover Frederick’s history. Just remember\, it’s much easier to laugh at a ghost story when you’re not sitting on the top deck in the dark. TOUR HIGHLIGHTS Hear researched tales of Frederick’s haunted places\, local legends and darker history\, told where the stories happened. Experience Frederick after dark from the top deck\, with historic streets\, autumn displays and a few places you’ll look at rather differently afterwards. TOUR DETAILS Price: $35 per person Duration: 1 hour Recommended Age: 14+ Departure: RAK Brewing Co\, 400 Sagner Ave\, Frederick\, MD\, 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/legends-%26-lore/26224/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventbloomsandbovines7chighlandcows2bpumpkinfloralcenterpieceevent25730-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261019T165505Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Blooms and Bovines | Highland Cows + Pumpkin Floral Centerpiece Event
DESCRIPTION:Blooms & Bovines: Fall Edition I can easily argue that fall on the farm is one of our favorite seasons - and this event is a big reason why!! “Blooms & Bovines: Fall Edition” is all about pumpkins\, florals and getting hands on with Highland cows! Your 1.5 hour time-slot on the farm will include: One pie pumpkin (varieties/colors will vary\, you get your pick!) A DIY flower bar to create a floral centerpiece with your pumpkin Hands on time with real life highland cows Photo opportunity with highland calf at our fall themed backdrop All flowers\, clippers cow brushes and supplies are included During the 1.5 hour time-slot on the farm\, the cows will be available for brushing for the first hour ONLY. The cows will be on break the remaining 30 minutes of your experience- the perfect time to finish your pumpkin centerpiece! $45/ticket - pre purchased tickets required. Every individual ages 4+ are required to have their own ticket regardless of participation level. Questions? Victoria at blackrockhighlands@gmail.com
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/blooms-and-bovines-%7c-highland-cows-%2b-pumpkin-floral-centerpiece-event/25730/
END:VEVENT
